{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794559949657,"sessionID":"ses_e2be4957affeeyAcLkZG48Stad","part":{"partID":"prt_1d41bb9e1001grJ7NRQEjPQYgX","sessionID":"ses_e2be4957affeeyAcLkZG48Stad","messageID":"msg_1d41b93e0001Bo2HipIkLqbGsb","type":"tool","id":"call_e66e9038d7f54e6ca71ee2c1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt, lines 1-288\n1: # /doctor:agents-md Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:agents-md <target>`: the argument failure, the startup menu, the check table, the embed and restore plans and their questions, result templates and next-step text. The command router owns target resolution and asset loading. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Argument Failure\n6: \n7: Every argument failure happens before any workflow YAML loads, prints the wording below with the bracketed parts filled in, and ends with the status line. Nothing is read and nothing is changed.\n8: \n9: | Situation | Wording |\n10: |-----------|---------|\n11: | The first token is not a target | `Unknown target: [target]` then `/doctor:agents-md runs check. Try: /doctor:agents-md menu` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_target\"` |\n12: | A flag none of the three targets accepts | `Unknown argument: [argument]` then `check accepts --json and --root <dir>; embed accepts --dry-run, --root <dir>, --plan-digest <digest>, --keep-claude-md, --remove-claude-md and --create-router; restore accepts --run <dir>, --yes and --dry-run.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n13: | A flag another target owns | `Argument '[argument]' is not valid for target '[target]'. Did you mean /doctor:agents-md [suggested-target] [argument]?` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"cross_target_flag\"` |\n14: | A value flag given without its value, such as `--plan-digest` or `--root` at the end of the line | `Missing value: [argument] needs [a directory for --root, the digest the plan printed for --plan-digest, the backup directory one apply printed for --run]` then `Try: [the accepted invocation for the bound target]` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"missing_argument\"` |\n15: | A target bound with a second positional (`check foo`, `embed foo`, `restore foo`) | `Only one target may be bound.` then `Try: /doctor:agents-md check [--json] [--root <dir>] for check, /doctor:agents-md embed [--dry-run] for embed, /doctor:agents-md restore --run=<dir> for restore` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"too_many_arguments\"` |\n16: | `restore` with no run directory | `Restore needs --run=<dir>, the backup directory one apply printed.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"missing_run_dir\"` |\n17: | An engine invoked with a subcommand or option it does not take | `USAGE: [the engine's first message line]` then the engine's usage block, exit 2. The workflow only ever runs the documented calls, so this is the engine's own contract rather than a route the operator reaches |\n18: \n19: ## 2. Startup Presentation\n20: \n21: This command is always interactive and has no `:auto` mode. With no target, `check` runs because it only reads, so a bare invocation needs no answer. The menu below appears for `menu`, `list` and `?`. Ask it once, then wait.\n22: \n23: ```text\n24: What do you want to do?\n25: \n26: 1) check\n27: 2) embed\n28: 3) restore\n29: X) Cancel\n30: ```\n31: \n32: Accepted answers:\n33: \n34: | Answer | Result | Meaning |\n35: |--------|--------|---------|\n36: | `1` | target = `check` | Report rows A1 to A12 for one repository's root instruction file and change nothing |\n37: | `2` | target = `embed` | Compose the shipped sections plus the repository block, show the plan and its digest, and write only on yes |\n38: | `3` | target = `restore` | Put back the paths one recorded run wrote, after its plan and one yes |\n39: | `X`, empty, `cancel` | `STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled` | Stop. Nothing changes |\n40: \n41: On any other response, re-emit the menu once. On a second invalid response, return `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_selection\"`.\n42: \n43: Valid targets: check, embed, restore\n44: \n45: ### Route Manifest Display\n46: \n47: Render this table for `menu`, `list` or `?`. Values mirror `_routes.yaml`.\n48: \n49: | Target | Workflow | Mutation Class | One-Line Purpose |\n50: |--------|----------|----------------|------------------|\n51: | `check` | `doctor-agents-md-check.yaml` | read-only | Report what the root instruction file holds against the shipped template, row by row |\n52: | `embed` | `doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml` | mutates | Bring the root instruction file up to the template after a plan, a digest and one yes |\n53: | `restore` | `doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml` | mutates | Put back exactly the paths one recorded run wrote |\n54: \n55: ## 3. Check Results\n56: \n57: The engine prints one line per row, A1 to A12, each carrying its own status and detail, then the result line. Quote the line rather than paraphrasing it, and lead the reply with the rows whose status is not `PASS`.\n58: \n59: `PASS` holds, `FINDING` fails, `UNKNOWN` means the row could not be answered and no pass was inferred, and `INFO` reports a fact the row does not grade.\n60: \n61: ```text\n62: Agents instruction check: [the root the engine read]\n63: \n64: A1  [PASS|FINDING|UNKNOWN|INFO]  install state: [pure|adopted|stale|forked|foreign|claude-only|absent]\n65: A2  [PASS|FINDING|UNKNOWN|INFO]  sections present: [n]/[n] matched\n66: ...\n67: A12 [PASS|FINDING|UNKNOWN|INFO]  template purity: [detail]\n68: STATUS=[OK|FINDINGS|UNKNOWN]\n69: ```\n70: \n71: The twelve rows are A1 install state, A2 sections present, A3 order and numbering, A4 section currency, A5 pins, A6 delivery budget, A7 repo-local block, A8 unmarked repo-unique content, A9 unmarked local edits, A10 runtime copies, A11 REPO RULES.md and A12 template purity. Read A1 first: it says which state the repository is in, and every other row is a detail of that state. A8 and A9 are the two rows that name a line somebody wrote, so quote them in full.\n72: \n73: With `--json` print the engine's JSON and nothing else: no table, no summary, no next-step line. The JSON carries the state, the twelve rows with their own status and detail, and the finding and unknown counts.\n74: \n75: ### Check Summary\n76: \n77: ```text\n78: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n79: Target: check\n80: Status: [OK|FINDINGS|UNKNOWN|ERROR]\n81: Mutation class: read-only\n82: Scope: [the root the engine read]\n83: Evidence: [n] rows, [n] pass, [n] findings, [n] unknown, [n] info\n84: Recommendation: [the repair for each finding, or none]\n85: STATUS=[status]\n86: ```\n87: \n88: Statuses this route prints, each on its own line so a workflow never has to compose one:\n89: \n90: ```text\n91: STATUS=OK\n92: STATUS=FINDINGS\n93: STATUS=UNKNOWN\n94: STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n95: ```\n96: \n97: An engine exit 1 with `findings=0` ends `STATUS=UNKNOWN`, never `STATUS=FINDINGS`: no finding was made, a row could not be answered, and the reply names that row and the precondition it is missing rather than sending the operator after a fault that was never found.\n98: \n99: ## 4. Embed Plan, Digest and Approval\n100: \n101: ### Setup\n102: \n103: Render this compact panel after target resolution and before the plan, when the target or flags were non-trivial.\n104: \n105: ```text\n106: DOCTOR ROUTE SETUP\n107: Target: embed\n108: Workflow: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n109: Mutation class: mutates\n110: Execution mode: INTERACTIVE\n111: Root: [the repository the run composes for]\n112: Presentation: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n113: Next: run the plan, which writes nothing\n114: ```\n115: \n116: ### The Plan The Operator Approves\n117: \n118: The plan section quotes the engine's own lines: its `[agents-md-embed] plan for <root> (state: <state>)` line, one `target <path>: <create|replace|remove|unchanged|absent>` line per path, its `note:` lines, a `diff` per path it would write, the new block between its `block:` and `block-end:` markers, the `budget:` line, each `finding:` line, the `preservation:` line, the `backup:` folder, its `backup-fallback:` line when one prints, the `undo:` command and the `plan-digest:` line. `absent` means the path is not there, so nothing is written to it and the note beside it says why it stays absent.\n119: \n120: ```text\n121: AGENTS INSTRUCTION EMBED PLAN\n122: Root: [the repository]\n123: State: [pure|adopted|stale|forked|foreign|claude-only|absent]\n124: Targets: [one line per target the engine printed, in its order]\n125: Notes: [one bullet per note, or none]\n126: Block: [the composed block, quoted whole]\n127: Budget: [the engine's budget line]\n128: Findings: [one bullet per finding line, or none]\n129: Preservation: [the engine's preservation line]\n130: Backup folder: [the engine's backup line]\n131: Backup note: [the engine's backup-fallback line, or none: it says why the folder sits outside the repository]\n132: Undo: [the engine's undo line]\n133: Plan digest: [the engine's plan-digest line]\n134: \n135: Embed these files now? [yes/no]\n136: ```\n137: \n138: The digest is not decoration: the digest on screen is the digest the apply repeats, and an apply whose digest no longer matches writes nothing. Show it in full, immediately above the question, and never compose a plan digest of your own.\n139: \n140: A plan whose repository already matches the template prints `[agents-md-embed] plan for <root> (state: <state>)` and `NOTHING TO DO` with no target lines. Render the unchanged result and ask nothing.\n141: \n142: ### Dry Run\n143: \n144: With `--dry-run`, follow the plan and the digest with `Dry run: nothing was written and nothing was asked.` and end with `STATUS=OK`. No question is asked and nothing is written.\n145: \n146: ### The Embed Question\n147: \n148: `Embed these files now? [yes/no]` covers the whole write: every path the plan names, the router rows it would add, the backup folder and the digest. Any answer other than yes counts as no: print the cancelled result and write nothing.\n149: \n150: ## 5. Restore Plan and Approval\n151: \n152: The restore plan is the engine's own dry run of one run's record, so it names what will be put back, what will be removed, and each folder that removal leaves empty.\n153: \n154: ```text\n155: AGENTS INSTRUCTION RESTORE PLAN\n156: Run directory: [the --run directory]\n157: Root: [the root the record names]\n158: Put back: [one line per recorded file, in the engine's order]\n159: Remove: [one line per path the recorded run created, or none]\n160: Already absent: [one line per path the recorded run created and that is already gone, or none]\n161: Folders: [one line per folder the recorded run created and an empty restore removes, or none]\n162: \n163: Restore these paths from that backup now? [yes/no]\n164: ```\n165: \n166: A recorded `AGENTS.md` that did not exist before the embed shows `delete` with the engine's own note: without it, Gate 3 no longer detects that directory as a workspace root. Quote that note.\n167: \n168: A folder the recorded run had to create for a new file gets its own folder line, and the restore removes it only once it is empty again. The line names the folder, never its contents.\n169: \n170: A record that names another root never reaches this plan: the restore refuses it before printing a line, says which root the record names, and writes nothing.\n171: \n172: `Restore these paths from that backup now? [yes/no]` covers the whole restore. Any answer other than yes counts as no: print the cancelled result and write nothing. The `--yes` flag is passed only after that yes, so the operator confirms once and the engine's own confirmation is satisfied by it.\n173: \n174: ## 6. Result Templates\n175: \n176: ### Embedded\n177: \n178: ```text\n179: DOCTOR MUTATING RESULT\n180: Target: embed\n181: Root: [the repository]\n182: Files changed: [each path the apply printed as wrote or removed]\n183: Pointer sync: [the engine's pointer-sync line]\n184: Router: [the engine's repo-rules line, or none when no router was written]\n185: Backup: [the engine's backup line]\n186: Re-read: [the check engine's result line and any row that still reports FINDING]\n187: Preservation: [the engine's preservation line]\n188: Undo: [the engine's undo block, quoted whole: its Undo: line, its restore command and one copy line per overwritten file]\n189: Next: [the repair the lines above name, or none: a nonzero pointer-sync ends here with /doctor:runtime-mirrors]\n190: STATUS=OK\n191: ```\n192: \n193: A nonzero `pointer-sync` line is not a verified mirror, and the run's `STATUS=OK` covers the files it wrote and nothing else. The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so on a repository that has no such file the line reads `exit 1 … missing` and the file is still absent when the run ends: it is never one of the files this run wrote, it never appears in `Files changed`, and the allowlist naming it is not evidence that it was written. Show `Pointer sync:` exactly as the engine printed it, show the run's own `STATUS=OK`, and let `Next:` carry the route that names the drifting mirror: `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`. What has to happen before that mirror can be written is in the troubleshooting table, because the file has to exist before the generator has a block to put in it.\n194: \n195: ### Unchanged\n196: \n197: Render this when the engine reports `NOTHING TO DO`.\n198: \n199: ```text\n200: DOCTOR TARGET UNCHANGED\n201: Target: embed\n202: Root: [the repository]\n203: State: [the engine's plan line]\n204: Changed: none\n205: STATUS=OK\n206: ```\n207: \n208: ### Cancelled\n209: \n210: Render this when the operator declines either question, and name what was declined.\n211: \n212: ```text\n213: DOCTOR TARGET CANCELLED\n214: Target: [embed|restore]\n215: Declined: [the embed | the restore]\n216: Changed: none\n217: STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled\n218: ```\n219: \n220: ### Dry Run\n221: \n222: ```text\n223: DOCTOR DRY RUN\n224: Target: [embed|restore]\n225: Plan: [the engine's plan lines, quoted as printed]\n226: Dry run: nothing was written and nothing was asked.\n227: Changed: none\n228: STATUS=OK\n229: ```\n230: \n231: ### Restored\n232: \n233: ```text\n234: DOCTOR MUTATING RESULT\n235: Target: restore\n236: Run directory: [the --run directory]\n237: Put back: [each path the restore printed as restored, or none]\n238: Removed: [each path it printed as removed, or none]\n239: Folders: [each folder it printed as removed, or none]\n240: Re-read: [the check engine's result line]\n241: STATUS=OK\n242: ```\n243: \n244: ### Failure Summary\n245: \n246: ```text\n247: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n248: Target: [check|embed|restore]\n249: Step: [the phase or row that stopped the run]\n250: Error: [the engine's code and message]\n251: Changed: [what was written before the failure, or none]\n252: Next: [the repair, or the accepted invocation]\n253: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"\n254: ```\n255: \n256: A check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing.\n257: \n258: ## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n259: \n260: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n261: |-----------|------------------|\n262: | A check row reports `FINDING` | Read that row's detail, fix that one requirement, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` |\n263: | A check row reports `UNKNOWN` | The row could not be answered, not failed. Rerun when its precondition is back, and never report an `UNKNOWN` row as a pass |\n264: | `A1` reports `stale`, `forked` or `foreign` | `/doctor:agents-md embed` shows what the run would compose and what it would carry before anything is written |\n265: | `A8` or `A9` reports content | The lines are the repository's own. An embed carries them into the block. A line that must stay routed belongs in a rule file authored through the create-repo-rule route |\n266: | `A6` reports a budget finding | The composed document is past the byte ceiling a truncating runtime stops at. Every carried line is still kept, and the finding is the operator's to resolve |\n267: | `A11` reports missing router rows | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds the shipped rows that are missing and touches no other row |\n268: | `A10` reports a runtime copy out of sync, or the apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so a missing file stays missing however often the embed reruns. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` lists the generated runtime mirrors that drift, each with the write form of the checker that owns it; the pointer block is not one of the files that route checks, so a `missing` line on it means the file has to exist first. Create `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --root <root>`, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` and read `A10` again |\n269: | The embed question was answered no | Nothing was written. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` when the plan is acceptable |\n270: | The apply reports a digest that does not match | The tree changed after the plan. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` so the plan and the digest describe the tree in front of you |\n271: | The apply reports a dropped line | The engine restored from the backup by itself. Read the dropped line, keep it in the block or in a reference document, then rerun the plan |\n272: | The embed is not wanted after all | `/doctor:agents-md restore --run=<the backup folder the apply printed>` puts back the files that run wrote |\n273: | A restore reports a hash that does not match | The record or one of its copies changed, so nothing was written. Read the message. The backup at that directory is kept |\n274: | A restore reports that the record names another root | The record belongs to the folder it names, and nothing was written. Rerun the restore with `--root <the root the record names>`, in the spaced form: `--root=` is not accepted |\n275: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n276: \n277: ## 8. Next Step\n278: \n279: | Condition | Suggested Command | Reason |\n280: |-----------|-------------------|--------|\n281: | A check row still reports `FINDING` after an embed | `/doctor:agents-md check` | The write is complete, and the remaining row is a different requirement |\n282: | The composed document is past the byte ceiling | `/doctor:agents-md check` | A6 names the ceiling and what the run kept anyway |\n283: | The repository has no `REPO RULES.md` | `/doctor:agents-md embed --create-router` | The router is created from the shipped rows and the checker runs after it |\n284: | The apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | It lists each generated runtime mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker, and `A10` names the copy that is still unverified |\n285: | A rule belongs in a routed file rather than the always-on block | `/create:repo-rule` | Action-triggered rules belong in a rule file that `REPO RULES.md` routes, not in a document every agent loads |\n286: | A release unit or a `.skilled/**` path needs changing | `/doctor:update` | This command owns the root instruction files, and the release tree belongs to the updater |\n287: \n288: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt, lines 1-288\n1: # /doctor:agents-md Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:agents-md <target>`: the argument failure, the startup menu, the check table, the embed and restore plans and their questions, result templates and next-step text. The command router owns target resolution and asset loading. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Argument Failure\n6: \n7: Every argument failure happens before any workflow YAML loads, prints the wording below with the bracketed parts filled in, and ends with the status line. Nothing is read and nothing is changed.\n8: \n9: | Situation | Wording |\n10: |-----------|---------|\n11: | The first token is not a target | `Unknown target: [target]` then `/doctor:agents-md runs check. Try: /doctor:agents-md menu` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_target\"` |\n12: | A flag none of the three targets accepts | `Unknown argument: [argument]` then `check accepts --json and --root <dir>; embed accepts --dry-run, --root <dir>, --plan-digest <digest>, --keep-claude-md, --remove-claude-md and --create-router; restore accepts --run <dir>, --yes and --dry-run.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n13: | A flag another target owns | `Argument '[argument]' is not valid for target '[target]'. Did you mean /doctor:agents-md [suggested-target] [argument]?` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"cross_target_flag\"` |\n14: | A value flag given without its value, such as `--plan-digest` or `--root` at the end of the line | `Missing value: [argument] needs [a directory for --root, the digest the plan printed for --plan-digest, the backup directory one apply printed for --run]` then `Try: [the accepted invocation for the bound target]` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"missing_argument\"` |\n15: | A target bound with a second positional (`check foo`, `embed foo`, `restore foo`) | `Only one target may be bound.` then `Try: /doctor:agents-md check [--json] [--root <dir>] for check, /doctor:agents-md embed [--dry-run] for embed, /doctor:agents-md restore --run=<dir> for restore` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"too_many_arguments\"` |\n16: | `restore` with no run directory | `Restore needs --run=<dir>, the backup directory one apply printed.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"missing_run_dir\"` |\n17: | An engine invoked with a subcommand or option it does not take | `USAGE: [the engine's first message line]` then the engine's usage block, exit 2. The workflow only ever runs the documented calls, so this is the engine's own contract rather than a route the operator reaches |\n18: \n19: ## 2. Startup Presentation\n20: \n21: This command is always interactive and has no `:auto` mode. With no target, `check` runs because it only reads, so a bare invocation needs no answer. The menu below appears for `menu`, `list` and `?`. Ask it once, then wait.\n22: \n23: ```text\n24: What do you want to do?\n25: \n26: 1) check\n27: 2) embed\n28: 3) restore\n29: X) Cancel\n30: ```\n31: \n32: Accepted answers:\n33: \n34: | Answer | Result | Meaning |\n35: |--------|--------|---------|\n36: | `1` | target = `check` | Report rows A1 to A12 for one repository's root instruction file and change nothing |\n37: | `2` | target = `embed` | Compose the shipped sections plus the repository block, show the plan and its digest, and write only on yes |\n38: | `3` | target = `restore` | Put back the paths one recorded run wrote, after its plan and one yes |\n39: | `X`, empty, `cancel` | `STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled` | Stop. Nothing changes |\n40: \n41: On any other response, re-emit the menu once. On a second invalid response, return `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_selection\"`.\n42: \n43: Valid targets: check, embed, restore\n44: \n45: ### Route Manifest Display\n46: \n47: Render this table for `menu`, `list` or `?`. Values mirror `_routes.yaml`.\n48: \n49: | Target | Workflow | Mutation Class | One-Line Purpose |\n50: |--------|----------|----------------|------------------|\n51: | `check` | `doctor-agents-md-check.yaml` | read-only | Report what the root instruction file holds against the shipped template, row by row |\n52: | `embed` | `doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml` | mutates | Bring the root instruction file up to the template after a plan, a digest and one yes |\n53: | `restore` | `doctor-agents-md-restore.yaml` | mutates | Put back exactly the paths one recorded run wrote |\n54: \n55: ## 3. Check Results\n56: \n57: The engine prints one line per row, A1 to A12, each carrying its own status and detail, then the result line. Quote the line rather than paraphrasing it, and lead the reply with the rows whose status is not `PASS`.\n58: \n59: `PASS` holds, `FINDING` fails, `UNKNOWN` means the row could not be answered and no pass was inferred, and `INFO` reports a fact the row does not grade.\n60: \n61: ```text\n62: Agents instruction check: [the root the engine read]\n63: \n64: A1  [PASS|FINDING|UNKNOWN|INFO]  install state: [pure|adopted|stale|forked|foreign|claude-only|absent]\n65: A2  [PASS|FINDING|UNKNOWN|INFO]  sections present: [n]/[n] matched\n66: ...\n67: A12 [PASS|FINDING|UNKNOWN|INFO]  template purity: [detail]\n68: STATUS=[OK|FINDINGS|UNKNOWN]\n69: ```\n70: \n71: The twelve rows are A1 install state, A2 sections present, A3 order and numbering, A4 section currency, A5 pins, A6 delivery budget, A7 repo-local block, A8 unmarked repo-unique content, A9 unmarked local edits, A10 runtime copies, A11 REPO RULES.md and A12 template purity. Read A1 first: it says which state the repository is in, and every other row is a detail of that state. A8 and A9 are the two rows that name a line somebody wrote, so quote them in full.\n72: \n73: With `--json` print the engine's JSON and nothing else: no table, no summary, no next-step line. The JSON carries the state, the twelve rows with their own status and detail, and the finding and unknown counts.\n74: \n75: ### Check Summary\n76: \n77: ```text\n78: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n79: Target: check\n80: Status: [OK|FINDINGS|UNKNOWN|ERROR]\n81: Mutation class: read-only\n82: Scope: [the root the engine read]\n83: Evidence: [n] rows, [n] pass, [n] findings, [n] unknown, [n] info\n84: Recommendation: [the repair for each finding, or none]\n85: STATUS=[status]\n86: ```\n87: \n88: Statuses this route prints, each on its own line so a workflow never has to compose one:\n89: \n90: ```text\n91: STATUS=OK\n92: STATUS=FINDINGS\n93: STATUS=UNKNOWN\n94: STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"\n95: ```\n96: \n97: An engine exit 1 with `findings=0` ends `STATUS=UNKNOWN`, never `STATUS=FINDINGS`: no finding was made, a row could not be answered, and the reply names that row and the precondition it is missing rather than sending the operator after a fault that was never found.\n98: \n99: ## 4. Embed Plan, Digest and Approval\n100: \n101: ### Setup\n102: \n103: Render this compact panel after target resolution and before the plan, when the target or flags were non-trivial.\n104: \n105: ```text\n106: DOCTOR ROUTE SETUP\n107: Target: embed\n108: Workflow: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n109: Mutation class: mutates\n110: Execution mode: INTERACTIVE\n111: Root: [the repository the run composes for]\n112: Presentation: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n113: Next: run the plan, which writes nothing\n114: ```\n115: \n116: ### The Plan The Operator Approves\n117: \n118: The plan section quotes the engine's own lines: its `[agents-md-embed] plan for <root> (state: <state>)` line, one `target <path>: <create|replace|remove|unchanged|absent>` line per path, its `note:` lines, a `diff` per path it would write, the new block between its `block:` and `block-end:` markers, the `budget:` line, each `finding:` line, the `preservation:` line, the `backup:` folder, its `backup-fallback:` line when one prints, the `undo:` command and the `plan-digest:` line. `absent` means the path is not there, so nothing is written to it and the note beside it says why it stays absent.\n119: \n120: ```text\n121: AGENTS INSTRUCTION EMBED PLAN\n122: Root: [the repository]\n123: State: [pure|adopted|stale|forked|foreign|claude-only|absent]\n124: Targets: [one line per target the engine printed, in its order]\n125: Notes: [one bullet per note, or none]\n126: Block: [the composed block, quoted whole]\n127: Budget: [the engine's budget line]\n128: Findings: [one bullet per finding line, or none]\n129: Preservation: [the engine's preservation line]\n130: Backup folder: [the engine's backup line]\n131: Backup note: [the engine's backup-fallback line, or none: it says why the folder sits outside the repository]\n132: Undo: [the engine's undo line]\n133: Plan digest: [the engine's plan-digest line]\n134: \n135: Embed these files now? [yes/no]\n136: ```\n137: \n138: The digest is not decoration: the digest on screen is the digest the apply repeats, and an apply whose digest no longer matches writes nothing. Show it in full, immediately above the question, and never compose a plan digest of your own.\n139: \n140: A plan whose repository already matches the template prints `[agents-md-embed] plan for <root> (state: <state>)` and `NOTHING TO DO` with no target lines. Render the unchanged result and ask nothing.\n141: \n142: ### Dry Run\n143: \n144: With `--dry-run`, follow the plan and the digest with `Dry run: nothing was written and nothing was asked.` and end with `STATUS=OK`. No question is asked and nothing is written.\n145: \n146: ### The Embed Question\n147: \n148: `Embed these files now? [yes/no]` covers the whole write: every path the plan names, the router rows it would add, the backup folder and the digest. Any answer other than yes counts as no: print the cancelled result and write nothing.\n149: \n150: ## 5. Restore Plan and Approval\n151: \n152: The restore plan is the engine's own dry run of one run's record, so it names what will be put back, what will be removed, and each folder that removal leaves empty.\n153: \n154: ```text\n155: AGENTS INSTRUCTION RESTORE PLAN\n156: Run directory: [the --run directory]\n157: Root: [the root the record names]\n158: Put back: [one line per recorded file, in the engine's order]\n159: Remove: [one line per path the recorded run created, or none]\n160: Already absent: [one line per path the recorded run created and that is already gone, or none]\n161: Folders: [one line per folder the recorded run created and an empty restore removes, or none]\n162: \n163: Restore these paths from that backup now? [yes/no]\n164: ```\n165: \n166: A recorded `AGENTS.md` that did not exist before the embed shows `delete` with the engine's own note: without it, Gate 3 no longer detects that directory as a workspace root. Quote that note.\n167: \n168: A folder the recorded run had to create for a new file gets its own folder line, and the restore removes it only once it is empty again. The line names the folder, never its contents.\n169: \n170: A record that names another root never reaches this plan: the restore refuses it before printing a line, says which root the record names, and writes nothing.\n171: \n172: `Restore these paths from that backup now? [yes/no]` covers the whole restore. Any answer other than yes counts as no: print the cancelled result and write nothing. The `--yes` flag is passed only after that yes, so the operator confirms once and the engine's own confirmation is satisfied by it.\n173: \n174: ## 6. Result Templates\n175: \n176: ### Embedded\n177: \n178: ```text\n179: DOCTOR MUTATING RESULT\n180: Target: embed\n181: Root: [the repository]\n182: Files changed: [each path the apply printed as wrote or removed]\n183: Pointer sync: [the engine's pointer-sync line]\n184: Router: [the engine's repo-rules line, or none when no router was written]\n185: Backup: [the engine's backup line]\n186: Re-read: [the check engine's result line and any row that still reports FINDING]\n187: Preservation: [the engine's preservation line]\n188: Undo: [the engine's undo block, quoted whole: its Undo: line, its restore command and one copy line per overwritten file]\n189: Next: [the repair the lines above name, or none: a nonzero pointer-sync ends here with /doctor:runtime-mirrors]\n190: STATUS=OK\n191: ```\n192: \n193: A nonzero `pointer-sync` line is not a verified mirror, and the run's `STATUS=OK` covers the files it wrote and nothing else. The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so on a repository that has no such file the line reads `exit 1 … missing` and the file is still absent when the run ends: it is never one of the files this run wrote, it never appears in `Files changed`, and the allowlist naming it is not evidence that it was written. Show `Pointer sync:` exactly as the engine printed it, show the run's own `STATUS=OK`, and let `Next:` carry the route that names the drifting mirror: `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`. What has to happen before that mirror can be written is in the troubleshooting table, because the file has to exist before the generator has a block to put in it.\n194: \n195: ### Unchanged\n196: \n197: Render this when the engine reports `NOTHING TO DO`.\n198: \n199: ```text\n200: DOCTOR TARGET UNCHANGED\n201: Target: embed\n202: Root: [the repository]\n203: State: [the engine's plan line]\n204: Changed: none\n205: STATUS=OK\n206: ```\n207: \n208: ### Cancelled\n209: \n210: Render this when the operator declines either question, and name what was declined.\n211: \n212: ```text\n213: DOCTOR TARGET CANCELLED\n214: Target: [embed|restore]\n215: Declined: [the embed | the restore]\n216: Changed: none\n217: STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled\n218: ```\n219: \n220: ### Dry Run\n221: \n222: ```text\n223: DOCTOR DRY RUN\n224: Target: [embed|restore]\n225: Plan: [the engine's plan lines, quoted as printed]\n226: Dry run: nothing was written and nothing was asked.\n227: Changed: none\n228: STATUS=OK\n229: ```\n230: \n231: ### Restored\n232: \n233: ```text\n234: DOCTOR MUTATING RESULT\n235: Target: restore\n236: Run directory: [the --run directory]\n237: Put back: [each path the restore printed as restored, or none]\n238: Removed: [each path it printed as removed, or none]\n239: Folders: [each folder it printed as removed, or none]\n240: Re-read: [the check engine's result line]\n241: STATUS=OK\n242: ```\n243: \n244: ### Failure Summary\n245: \n246: ```text\n247: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n248: Target: [check|embed|restore]\n249: Step: [the phase or row that stopped the run]\n250: Error: [the engine's code and message]\n251: Changed: [what was written before the failure, or none]\n252: Next: [the repair, or the accepted invocation]\n253: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"\n254: ```\n255: \n256: A check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing.\n257: \n258: ## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n259: \n260: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n261: |-----------|------------------|\n262: | A check row reports `FINDING` | Read that row's detail, fix that one requirement, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` |\n263: | A check row reports `UNKNOWN` | The row could not be answered, not failed. Rerun when its precondition is back, and never report an `UNKNOWN` row as a pass |\n264: | `A1` reports `stale`, `forked` or `foreign` | `/doctor:agents-md embed` shows what the run would compose and what it would carry before anything is written |\n265: | `A8` or `A9` reports content | The lines are the repository's own. An embed carries them into the block. A line that must stay routed belongs in a rule file authored through the create-repo-rule route |\n266: | `A6` reports a budget finding | The composed document is past the byte ceiling a truncating runtime stops at. Every carried line is still kept, and the finding is the operator's to resolve |\n267: | `A11` reports missing router rows | `/doctor:agents-md embed` adds the shipped rows that are missing and touches no other row |\n268: | `A10` reports a runtime copy out of sync, or the apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | The generator rewrites an existing `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` and never creates a missing one, so a missing file stays missing however often the embed reruns. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` lists the generated runtime mirrors that drift, each with the write form of the checker that owns it; the pointer block is not one of the files that route checks, so a `missing` line on it means the file has to exist first. Create `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md`, run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs --root <root>`, then rerun `/doctor:agents-md check` and read `A10` again |\n269: | The embed question was answered no | Nothing was written. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` when the plan is acceptable |\n270: | The apply reports a digest that does not match | The tree changed after the plan. Rerun `/doctor:agents-md embed` so the plan and the digest describe the tree in front of you |\n271: | The apply reports a dropped line | The engine restored from the backup by itself. Read the dropped line, keep it in the block or in a reference document, then rerun the plan |\n272: | The embed is not wanted after all | `/doctor:agents-md restore --run=<the backup folder the apply printed>` puts back the files that run wrote |\n273: | A restore reports a hash that does not match | The record or one of its copies changed, so nothing was written. Read the message. The backup at that directory is kept |\n274: | A restore reports that the record names another root | The record belongs to the folder it names, and nothing was written. Rerun the restore with `--root <the root the record names>`, in the spaced form: `--root=` is not accepted |\n275: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n276: \n277: ## 8. Next Step\n278: \n279: | Condition | Suggested Command | Reason |\n280: |-----------|-------------------|--------|\n281: | A check row still reports `FINDING` after an embed | `/doctor:agents-md check` | The write is complete, and the remaining row is a different requirement |\n282: | The composed document is past the byte ceiling | `/doctor:agents-md check` | A6 names the ceiling and what the run kept anyway |\n283: | The repository has no `REPO RULES.md` | `/doctor:agents-md embed --create-router` | The router is created from the shipped rows and the checker runs after it |\n284: | The apply's `pointer-sync:` line reported a nonzero exit | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | It lists each generated runtime mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker, and `A10` names the copy that is still unverified |\n285: | A rule belongs in a routed file rather than the always-on block | `/create:repo-rule` | Action-triggered rules belong in a rule file that `REPO RULES.md` routes, not in a document every agent loads |\n286: | A release unit or a `.skilled/**` path needs changing | `/doctor:update` | This command owns the root instruction files, and the release tree belongs to the updater |\n287: \n288: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794559949282,"end":1794559949657}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794559949661,"sessionID":"ses_e2be4957affeeyAcLkZG48Stad","part":{"partID":"prt_1d41bb85b002Cy2XQ0XJofzyK9","sessionID":"ses_e2be4957affeeyAcLkZG48Stad","messageID":"msg_1d41b93e0001Bo2HipIkLqbGsb","type":"tool","id":"call_de89e022f3604ad9a1904356","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml, lines 1-130\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SHIPPED INSTRUCTION EMBED (INTERACTIVE, ONE REPOSITORY)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Careful operator bringing one repository's root instruction file up to the shipped template without losing a line the repository wrote\n5: purpose: Compose in memory, print the plan with its digest, ask once, write only after that yes and only against the digest the plan printed, then prove on disk that nothing was dropped and hand back the engine's own undo block\n6: action: Read the engine and the target -> run the plan -> show the plan, the diff, the budget and the digest -> explicit yes -> apply with that digest -> re-read the written files through the check engine -> print the engine's undo block\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: sequential_read_plan_confirmed_embed\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: interactive\n16:   approvals: explicit_yes\n17:   dry_run: print_the_plan_then_status_ok_without_asking\n18:   tracking: one_repository_root\n19:   validation: re_read_the_written_files_through_the_check_engine\n20:   never_commit: true\n21: \n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES\n24: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n25: mutation_boundaries:\n26:   read_only: false\n27:   allowed_targets:\n28:     - \"AGENTS.md, the root document: created when the repository has none, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block, and left alone when it already matches\"\n29:     - \"CLAUDE.md, folded into the block and replaced by a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer by default. Kept as it is, with its lines still moved into the block, when --keep-claude-md was given. Created as that pointer when it is absent and the run writes another file.\"\n30:     - \".codex/AGENTS.md, folded into the block and removed\"\n31:     - \".cursor/rules/repo-local.md, the generated mirror of a non-empty block; removed when the block is empty\"\n32:     - \".cursor/rules/skill-routing.md, rewritten by its own generator, sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, which this engine calls and never composes a byte of\"\n33:     - \"REPO RULES.md, the router: shipped rows that are missing are appended and no other row is touched, and a missing file is created only behind --create-router\"\n34:     - \"the backup directory the plan prints, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ or the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path: every path the run touches is copied there before the first write, and the record beside the copies is what restore reads\"\n35:   forbidden_targets:\n36:     - \"any path outside that allowlist, which the engine checks in code before every write rather than trusting this document\"\n37:     - \".skilled/**, which /doctor:update owns, including the manifest this engine reads\"\n38:     - \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs and its lib/, which own the composition and never change here\"\n39:     - \"a rule file a REPO RULES.md row points at, which is authored through the create-repo-rule route and never by this one\"\n40:     - \"the git index, history and remotes\"\n41:   invariant: \"Nothing is written until the plan has printed its digest and the operator has answered yes to that plan. The plan call composes in memory and writes nothing, the apply refuses a digest that no longer matches and writes nothing in that case, and every path the run touches is copied to the backup before the first byte. The proof that no repository line was dropped runs against the bytes now on disk, and a violation restores from the backup automatically. A no at the question ends the run with STATUS=CANCELLED and nothing written.\"\n42: \n43: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n44: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n45: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n46: upstream_assets:\n47:   embed_engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs\"\n48:   check_engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs\"\n49:   section_library: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/lib/agents-md-sections.cjs\"\n50:   template_manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\"\n51:   pointer_generator: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, called by the engine and never by this workflow\"\n52:   repo_rules_checker: \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-repo-rule/scripts/check-repo-rules.cjs, called by the engine after a router write\"\n53:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\"\n54: \n55: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: # INPUTS\n57: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n58: inputs:\n59:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n60:   root: \"The repository to compose for when --root <dir> is passed, resolved by the engine (default none, so the repository this command ships in).\"\n61:   dry_run: \"--dry-run prints the plan and its digest, then STATUS=OK without asking a question (default false). The plan call writes nothing either way; the flag only removes the question and the write.\"\n62:   plan_digest: \"The plan digest the plan printed. It is what makes the approved bytes checkable: the apply recomposes and refuses any digest that no longer matches.\"\n63:   digest_confirmation: \"true once the operator has answered yes to the plan whose digest was on screen. A plan approved at one tree is never applied at another, because the digest would not match.\"\n64:   keep_claude_md: \"--keep-claude-md folds a divergent CLAUDE.md into the block and keeps the file. --remove-claude-md folds it and leaves a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer, which is the default (default false, so the pointer).\"\n65:   create_router: \"--create-router creates REPO RULES.md from the shipped rows when it is missing (default false, so a missing router is a note and a finding).\"\n66: \n67: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n68: # WORKFLOW\n69: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n70: workflow:\n71:   phase_1_read:\n72:     purpose: \"Load what the run is built from before anything is composed or asked\"\n73:     activities:\n74:       - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/lib/agents-md-sections.cjs and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json exist. If any is missing, report the missing path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. An embed without its engine or its manifest would invent a template.\"\n75:       - \"Read the engine's interface before driving it: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs with no subcommand prints its usage block and exits 2, and that block is the whole list of calls this workflow may make. plan composes in memory and writes nothing. apply --plan-digest <digest> refuses a digest that does not match the composition and otherwise backs up, writes and proves. restore --run=<dir> puts back the paths one apply recorded. --dry-run prints a plan and writes nothing. --yes takes the confirmation as given.\"\n76:       - \"Read .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt for the plan, question, refusal and result wording. Every visible line comes from there.\"\n77:       - \"Read nothing out of the target to decide the composition. The three-way section classification, the block and the budget are the engine's answers, and a second reading here would be a second opinion that drifts from it.\"\n78: \n79:   phase_2_plan:\n80:     purpose: \"Run the read-only plan and keep its notes, its findings and its digest apart\"\n81:     activities:\n82:       - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs plan, adding --root \\\"{root}\\\" when the operator passed one, --keep-claude-md when the divergent copy is to be kept, --create-router when a missing router is to be created, and --dry-run when the operator asked for one. The plan call writes nothing: it composes every target in memory, prints each target with its action, the diff, the new block, the budget, the survival ledger, the backup folder and the plan digest.\"\n83:       - \"Keep the engine's exact lines: the target list with the action each target takes, absent included, each note, each diff, the block lines between the engine's `block:` and `block-end:` markers, the budget line, each finding line, the preservation line, the backup line, the backup-fallback line when one prints, the undo line and the plan-digest line. They are what the operator approves, and no other plan is ever the one this run applies.\"\n84:       - \"Exit 0 with NOTHING TO DO means the repository is already in its target state, which the engine prints without a plan. Render the presentation contract's unchanged result with the engine's own notes, ask nothing, write nothing and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK.\"\n85:       - \"A finding line that says the composed document is past the byte ceiling is a finding rather than a refusal: every carried line is kept, because preservation outranks the budget. Show it with the plan and let the operator decide. A run whose composition drops a line refuses instead, exits 1 and writes nothing; print the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL and stop.\"\n86:       - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own lines, print the dry-run line and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing and writes nothing, so it runs no question and no apply.\"\n87:       - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n88: \n89:   phase_3_approval:\n90:     purpose: \"Ask the one embed question against the plan on screen, and write only after its yes\"\n91:     activities:\n92:       - \"Ask the embed question once, in the presentation contract's wording, naming the files the plan will create, replace or remove, the backup folder, the router rows the plan would add and the plan digest. The operator answers about the plan the operator has just read, which is this run's plan.\"\n93:       - \"Any answer other than yes is a no: print the cancelled result naming the declined embed, state Changed: none, and end with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled. Nothing is written.\"\n94:       - \"Never default an answer, never carry an approval from an earlier run, and never accept a digest the operator has not seen. Phase 4 runs only after this phase's yes.\"\n95: \n96:   phase_4_write:\n97:     purpose: \"Write the approved composition and nothing else, only after the embed yes\"\n98:     activities:\n99:       - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs apply --plan-digest \\\"{plan_digest}\\\" with exactly the flags the plan ran with: --root \\\"{root}\\\" when it was given, --keep-claude-md or --remove-claude-md as approved, and --create-router when it was approved. Run it only after the embed yes.\"\n100:       - \"Exit 2 with a message that the plan digest does not match the composition now means the tree changed after the plan, so nothing was written. Quote the engine's message, offer the plan again against the current tree, and end with STATUS=FAIL. Never retry the apply with a recomposed digest of your own: the point of the digest is that the approved bytes are the written bytes.\"\n101:       - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n102:       - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n103:       - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line. The engine restored from the backup by itself and kept the backup. Quote the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n104:       - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n105: \n106:   phase_5_reread:\n107:     purpose: \"Prove the written repository reads back through the read-only engine\"\n108:     activities:\n109:       - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs once, with --root \\\"{root}\\\" when this run was pointed at another repository, and read the twelve rows against the plan's claims: the block the plan composed is the block on disk, and the paths the apply printed as written are the paths the check reads.\"\n110:       - \"The engine prints its own check-after line at the end of a successful apply. Keep that line and the re-read beside each other: two readings of the same tree disagreeing is a failure, not a warning.\"\n111:       - \"A row that still reports FINDING after a clean write is not a failed embed: the write completed and the row names a different requirement, so report it as the next step and keep the result at STATUS=OK.\"\n112:       - \"When the re-read cannot run at all, report its message, keep the write result, and name the missing check as the next step. Never report an embed as verified when the re-read never answered.\"\n113: \n114:   phase_6_report:\n115:     purpose: \"Summarize the run and hand the way back to the operator\"\n116:     activities:\n117:       - \"When the write ran and read back, render the presentation contract's embedded result with the paths the engine wrote or removed, the pointer-sync and repo-rules lines as they printed, the backup folder, the re-read verdict, the undo block the engine printed and the next line those lines name.\"\n118:       - \"Print the engine's undo block exactly as the apply printed it: its Undo: line, the restore command it names and the copy line per overwritten file, in that order and with no path shortened. Never compose an undo of this route's own and never run it here. Never run the undo inside this route.\"\n119:       - \"A no answered a question: render the cancelled result naming what was declined, state Changed: none and end with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled.\"\n120:       - \"A dry run: render the dry-run result with the plan, the digest and the dry-run line, and end with STATUS=OK.\"\n121:       - \"NOTHING TO DO: render the unchanged result with the engine's notes and STATUS=OK.\"\n122:       - \"A refusal, a missing asset, a dropped line or a digest mismatch stopped the run: render the failure result naming the phase and the engine's code, with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n123:       - \"End by saying the operator commits the written files themselves; this route stages and commits nothing.\"\n124: \n125: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n126: # OUTPUT\n127: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n128: output:\n129:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\"\n130:   statuses: [OK, CANCELLED, FAIL]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml, lines 1-130\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DOCTOR: SHIPPED INSTRUCTION EMBED (INTERACTIVE, ONE REPOSITORY)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: role: Careful operator bringing one repository's root instruction file up to the shipped template without losing a line the repository wrote\n5: purpose: Compose in memory, print the plan with its digest, ask once, write only after that yes and only against the digest the plan printed, then prove on disk that nothing was dropped and hand back the engine's own undo block\n6: action: Read the engine and the target -> run the plan -> show the plan, the diff, the budget and the digest -> explicit yes -> apply with that digest -> re-read the written files through the check engine -> print the engine's undo block\n7: skill_owner: \".skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/\"\n8: \n9: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: # OPERATING MODE\n11: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n12: operating_mode:\n13:   workflow: sequential_read_plan_confirmed_embed\n14:   compliance: MANDATORY\n15:   execution: interactive\n16:   approvals: explicit_yes\n17:   dry_run: print_the_plan_then_status_ok_without_asking\n18:   tracking: one_repository_root\n19:   validation: re_read_the_written_files_through_the_check_engine\n20:   never_commit: true\n21: \n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES\n24: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n25: mutation_boundaries:\n26:   read_only: false\n27:   allowed_targets:\n28:     - \"AGENTS.md, the root document: created when the repository has none, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block, and left alone when it already matches\"\n29:     - \"CLAUDE.md, folded into the block and replaced by a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer by default. Kept as it is, with its lines still moved into the block, when --keep-claude-md was given. Created as that pointer when it is absent and the run writes another file.\"\n30:     - \".codex/AGENTS.md, folded into the block and removed\"\n31:     - \".cursor/rules/repo-local.md, the generated mirror of a non-empty block; removed when the block is empty\"\n32:     - \".cursor/rules/skill-routing.md, rewritten by its own generator, sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, which this engine calls and never composes a byte of\"\n33:     - \"REPO RULES.md, the router: shipped rows that are missing are appended and no other row is touched, and a missing file is created only behind --create-router\"\n34:     - \"the backup directory the plan prints, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ or the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path: every path the run touches is copied there before the first write, and the record beside the copies is what restore reads\"\n35:   forbidden_targets:\n36:     - \"any path outside that allowlist, which the engine checks in code before every write rather than trusting this document\"\n37:     - \".skilled/**, which /doctor:update owns, including the manifest this engine reads\"\n38:     - \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs and its lib/, which own the composition and never change here\"\n39:     - \"a rule file a REPO RULES.md row points at, which is authored through the create-repo-rule route and never by this one\"\n40:     - \"the git index, history and remotes\"\n41:   invariant: \"Nothing is written until the plan has printed its digest and the operator has answered yes to that plan. The plan call composes in memory and writes nothing, the apply refuses a digest that no longer matches and writes nothing in that case, and every path the run touches is copied to the backup before the first byte. The proof that no repository line was dropped runs against the bytes now on disk, and a violation restores from the backup automatically. A no at the question ends the run with STATUS=CANCELLED and nothing written.\"\n42: \n43: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n44: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n45: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n46: upstream_assets:\n47:   embed_engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs\"\n48:   check_engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs\"\n49:   section_library: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/lib/agents-md-sections.cjs\"\n50:   template_manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json\"\n51:   pointer_generator: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, called by the engine and never by this workflow\"\n52:   repo_rules_checker: \".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-repo-rule/scripts/check-repo-rules.cjs, called by the engine after a router write\"\n53:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\"\n54: \n55: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: # INPUTS\n57: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n58: inputs:\n59:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n60:   root: \"The repository to compose for when --root <dir> is passed, resolved by the engine (default none, so the repository this command ships in).\"\n61:   dry_run: \"--dry-run prints the plan and its digest, then STATUS=OK without asking a question (default false). The plan call writes nothing either way; the flag only removes the question and the write.\"\n62:   plan_digest: \"The plan digest the plan printed. It is what makes the approved bytes checkable: the apply recomposes and refuses any digest that no longer matches.\"\n63:   digest_confirmation: \"true once the operator has answered yes to the plan whose digest was on screen. A plan approved at one tree is never applied at another, because the digest would not match.\"\n64:   keep_claude_md: \"--keep-claude-md folds a divergent CLAUDE.md into the block and keeps the file. --remove-claude-md folds it and leaves a one-line @AGENTS.md pointer, which is the default (default false, so the pointer).\"\n65:   create_router: \"--create-router creates REPO RULES.md from the shipped rows when it is missing (default false, so a missing router is a note and a finding).\"\n66: \n67: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n68: # WORKFLOW\n69: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n70: workflow:\n71:   phase_1_read:\n72:     purpose: \"Load what the run is built from before anything is composed or asked\"\n73:     activities:\n74:       - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/lib/agents-md-sections.cjs and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json exist. If any is missing, report the missing path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. An embed without its engine or its manifest would invent a template.\"\n75:       - \"Read the engine's interface before driving it: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs with no subcommand prints its usage block and exits 2, and that block is the whole list of calls this workflow may make. plan composes in memory and writes nothing. apply --plan-digest <digest> refuses a digest that does not match the composition and otherwise backs up, writes and proves. restore --run=<dir> puts back the paths one apply recorded. --dry-run prints a plan and writes nothing. --yes takes the confirmation as given.\"\n76:       - \"Read .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt for the plan, question, refusal and result wording. Every visible line comes from there.\"\n77:       - \"Read nothing out of the target to decide the composition. The three-way section classification, the block and the budget are the engine's answers, and a second reading here would be a second opinion that drifts from it.\"\n78: \n79:   phase_2_plan:\n80:     purpose: \"Run the read-only plan and keep its notes, its findings and its digest apart\"\n81:     activities:\n82:       - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs plan, adding --root \\\"{root}\\\" when the operator passed one, --keep-claude-md when the divergent copy is to be kept, --create-router when a missing router is to be created, and --dry-run when the operator asked for one. The plan call writes nothing: it composes every target in memory, prints each target with its action, the diff, the new block, the budget, the survival ledger, the backup folder and the plan digest.\"\n83:       - \"Keep the engine's exact lines: the target list with the action each target takes, absent included, each note, each diff, the block lines between the engine's `block:` and `block-end:` markers, the budget line, each finding line, the preservation line, the backup line, the backup-fallback line when one prints, the undo line and the plan-digest line. They are what the operator approves, and no other plan is ever the one this run applies.\"\n84:       - \"Exit 0 with NOTHING TO DO means the repository is already in its target state, which the engine prints without a plan. Render the presentation contract's unchanged result with the engine's own notes, ask nothing, write nothing and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK.\"\n85:       - \"A finding line that says the composed document is past the byte ceiling is a finding rather than a refusal: every carried line is kept, because preservation outranks the budget. Show it with the plan and let the operator decide. A run whose composition drops a line refuses instead, exits 1 and writes nothing; print the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL and stop.\"\n86:       - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own lines, print the dry-run line and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing and writes nothing, so it runs no question and no apply.\"\n87:       - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n88: \n89:   phase_3_approval:\n90:     purpose: \"Ask the one embed question against the plan on screen, and write only after its yes\"\n91:     activities:\n92:       - \"Ask the embed question once, in the presentation contract's wording, naming the files the plan will create, replace or remove, the backup folder, the router rows the plan would add and the plan digest. The operator answers about the plan the operator has just read, which is this run's plan.\"\n93:       - \"Any answer other than yes is a no: print the cancelled result naming the declined embed, state Changed: none, and end with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled. Nothing is written.\"\n94:       - \"Never default an answer, never carry an approval from an earlier run, and never accept a digest the operator has not seen. Phase 4 runs only after this phase's yes.\"\n95: \n96:   phase_4_write:\n97:     purpose: \"Write the approved composition and nothing else, only after the embed yes\"\n98:     activities:\n99:       - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs apply --plan-digest \\\"{plan_digest}\\\" with exactly the flags the plan ran with: --root \\\"{root}\\\" when it was given, --keep-claude-md or --remove-claude-md as approved, and --create-router when it was approved. Run it only after the embed yes.\"\n100:       - \"Exit 2 with a message that the plan digest does not match the composition now means the tree changed after the plan, so nothing was written. Quote the engine's message, offer the plan again against the current tree, and end with STATUS=FAIL. Never retry the apply with a recomposed digest of your own: the point of the digest is that the approved bytes are the written bytes.\"\n101:       - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n102:       - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n103:       - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line. The engine restored from the backup by itself and kept the backup. Quote the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n104:       - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n105: \n106:   phase_5_reread:\n107:     purpose: \"Prove the written repository reads back through the read-only engine\"\n108:     activities:\n109:       - \"Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs once, with --root \\\"{root}\\\" when this run was pointed at another repository, and read the twelve rows against the plan's claims: the block the plan composed is the block on disk, and the paths the apply printed as written are the paths the check reads.\"\n110:       - \"The engine prints its own check-after line at the end of a successful apply. Keep that line and the re-read beside each other: two readings of the same tree disagreeing is a failure, not a warning.\"\n111:       - \"A row that still reports FINDING after a clean write is not a failed embed: the write completed and the row names a different requirement, so report it as the next step and keep the result at STATUS=OK.\"\n112:       - \"When the re-read cannot run at all, report its message, keep the write result, and name the missing check as the next step. Never report an embed as verified when the re-read never answered.\"\n113: \n114:   phase_6_report:\n115:     purpose: \"Summarize the run and hand the way back to the operator\"\n116:     activities:\n117:       - \"When the write ran and read back, render the presentation contract's embedded result with the paths the engine wrote or removed, the pointer-sync and repo-rules lines as they printed, the backup folder, the re-read verdict, the undo block the engine printed and the next line those lines name.\"\n118:       - \"Print the engine's undo block exactly as the apply printed it: its Undo: line, the restore command it names and the copy line per overwritten file, in that order and with no path shortened. Never compose an undo of this route's own and never run it here. Never run the undo inside this route.\"\n119:       - \"A no answered a question: render the cancelled result naming what was declined, state Changed: none and end with STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled.\"\n120:       - \"A dry run: render the dry-run result with the plan, the digest and the dry-run line, and end with STATUS=OK.\"\n121:       - \"NOTHING TO DO: render the unchanged result with the engine's notes and STATUS=OK.\"\n122:       - \"A refusal, a missing asset, a dropped line or a digest mismatch stopped the run: render the failure result naming the phase and the engine's code, with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n123:       - \"End by saying the operator commits the written files themselves; this route stages and commits nothing.\"\n124: \n125: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n126: # OUTPUT\n127: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n128: output:\n129:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\"\n130:   statuses: [OK, CANCELLED, FAIL]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794559948892,"end":1794559949661}}}}
