{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794560032880,"sessionID":"ses_e2be4957affeeyAcLkZG48Stad","part":{"partID":"prt_1d41cfc54001dv6VC0EAAekeyc","sessionID":"ses_e2be4957affeeyAcLkZG48Stad","messageID":"msg_1d41cef07001ZcQQYFnWvNtkkI","type":"tool","id":"call_bd92b40cc7b84abab9b7b685","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt"},"output":" M .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n M .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\nindex d53dde5c4a..6fe597d842 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@ workflow:\n       - \"Exit 0 with NOTHING TO DO means the repository is already in its target state, which the engine prints without a plan. Render the presentation contract's unchanged result with the engine's own notes, ask nothing, write nothing and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK.\"\n       - \"A finding line that says the composed document is past the byte ceiling is a finding rather than a refusal: every carried line is kept, because preservation outranks the budget. Show it with the plan and let the operator decide. A run whose composition drops a line refuses instead, exits 1 and writes nothing; print the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL and stop.\"\n       - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own lines, print the dry-run line and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing and writes nothing, so it runs no question and no apply.\"\n-      - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n+      - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document, a symlinked REPO RULES.md or Cursor mirror the run would write, or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n \n   phase_3_approval:\n     purpose: \"Ask the one embed question against the plan on screen, and write only after its yes\"\n@@ -100,7 +100,8 @@ workflow:\n       - \"Exit 2 with a message that the plan digest does not match the composition now means the tree changed after the plan, so nothing was written. Quote the engine's message, offer the plan again against the current tree, and end with STATUS=FAIL. Never retry the apply with a recomposed digest of your own: the point of the digest is that the approved bytes are the written bytes.\"\n       - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n       - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n-      - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line. The engine restored from the backup by itself and kept the backup. Quote the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n+      - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line or a `foreign:` line. The engine restored from the backup by itself unless it printed `nothing was restored`, and kept the backup. Quote the lines the proof named, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it when the restore ran. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n+      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\"\n       - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n \n   phase_5_reread:\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\nindex b736a2e477..b08fe38e6e 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n@@ -253,7 +253,7 @@ Next: [the repair, or the accepted invocation]\n STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"\n ```\n \n-A check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing.\n+A check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing. An embed that exits 3 had a write fail after its backup. Its Changed: is none when the output holds restored:, and otherwise the reply says the tree is partly written and its Next: is the undo command the engine printed.\n \n ## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n \n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":" M .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n M .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\nindex d53dde5c4a..6fe597d842 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@ workflow:\n       - \"Exit 0 with NOTHING TO DO means the repository is already in its target state, which the engine prints without a plan. Render the presentation contract's unchanged result with the engine's own notes, ask nothing, write nothing and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK.\"\n       - \"A finding line that says the composed document is past the byte ceiling is a finding rather than a refusal: every carried line is kept, because preservation outranks the budget. Show it with the plan and let the operator decide. A run whose composition drops a line refuses instead, exits 1 and writes nothing; print the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL and stop.\"\n       - \"If dry_run is true, render the presentation contract's dry-run result from the plan's own lines, print the dry-run line and go to phase 6 with STATUS=OK. A dry run asks nothing and writes nothing, so it runs no question and no apply.\"\n-      - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n+      - \"Exit 2 means a precondition failed, such as a missing manifest, a symlinked root document, a symlinked REPO RULES.md or Cursor mirror the run would write, or one of the two markers present without the other. Quote the engine's message, name the accepted invocation (/doctor:agents-md embed), and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n \n   phase_3_approval:\n     purpose: \"Ask the one embed question against the plan on screen, and write only after its yes\"\n@@ -100,7 +100,8 @@ workflow:\n       - \"Exit 2 with a message that the plan digest does not match the composition now means the tree changed after the plan, so nothing was written. Quote the engine's message, offer the plan again against the current tree, and end with STATUS=FAIL. Never retry the apply with a recomposed digest of your own: the point of the digest is that the approved bytes are the written bytes.\"\n       - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n       - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n-      - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line. The engine restored from the backup by itself and kept the backup. Quote the dropped lines, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n+      - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line or a `foreign:` line. The engine restored from the backup by itself unless it printed `nothing was restored`, and kept the backup. Quote the lines the proof named, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it when the restore ran. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n+      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\"\n       - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n \n   phase_5_reread:\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\nindex b736a2e477..b08fe38e6e 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\n@@ -253,7 +253,7 @@ Next: [the repair, or the accepted invocation]\n STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[code]\"\n ```\n \n-A check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing.\n+A check that exits 2 prints its message and ends `STATUS=ERROR ERROR=\"[message]\"`. An embed that exits 1 after its proof found a dropped line restored from the backup by itself, so its `Changed:` is `none` and its `Next:` names the file whose line went missing. An embed that exits 3 had a write fail after its backup. Its Changed: is none when the output holds restored:, and otherwise the reply says the tree is partly written and its Next: is the undo command the engine printed.\n \n ## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n \n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794560031828,"end":1794560032880}}}}
